SUMMARY:UnRavel yo’self at Lower Big Hungry Falls
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\nI am going to unravel my stress at Lower Bi
 g Hungry Falls. There is a large sand beach that is popular in warm weathe
 r. ***Bring gloves. Bring 1 small grocery bag for litter pick-up..***\n**O
 ptional:** swimming. **Bring an inner tube float.**\nRemember . **Water sp
 rites are mischievous in the Summer.**\nWe will spend up to 2 hrs at the F
 alls. Come prepared to meditate\, practice your Tai-Chi\, **森林浴**\, 
 read a book\, prepare a meal\, play a flute.\nDifficulty: Natural trail w/
  rock & roots & 1 short steep section.\n**We are the Sloth Hiking Team of 
 WNC: “We will get there when we get there.” We dare to go where the 
 ‘real’ hike groups don’t !!**\n**https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Vqh
 CQZaH4Vs**\n**This is a designated ‘silent’ Relaxation Hike\; we will 
 engage quiet for the day. But "Ooh's and Aah's" are encouraged.**\nI will 
 spend (up to) 2 hours at the falls swimming\, eating\, reading\, ponderin
 ’ and pretending to meditate. (shorter durations optional)\n**Optional: 
 Pack yo’ lite-weight campchair.**\n**We are also doing lite clean-up mai
 ntenance.**\nIncessant prattlers will be assumed to be having an affair. O
 bstreperous raucous yawping is discouraged.\n**Hike Details:**\n**(Social 
 ‘hour’ at 9:45AM. Tires roll at 10:00AM**\nLength: 1.1 mi RT (in&out)\
 ; **Total descent: 325 ft (and return)**\n**Drive time: 20 min**\n**Return
  Apprx: 2:30 PM**\n**Carpool contributions appreciated. $2.00 suggested**\
 n**THIS IS A DOG-PARTICIPANT HIKE.** This event is NOT for those who are u
 ncomfortable with the antics of fun-loving dogs. Well trained dogs (you do
 n’t have to yell.) can be 'off-leash'. Small (lap)dogs may carpool. Larg
 e dogs will drive themselves.\nWeather Check: Hendersonville\nWAITLISTED P
 EOPLE WILL BE ADDED AS DRIVERS SIGN ON.\n(I currently have 2.5 driver(s). 
 (=10)\nWe suggest masks and open windows while carpooling. Only you know y
 our own health status so judge accordingly if an event may endanger your h
 ealth or the health of others.\nPlease bring an extra pair of shoes to avo
 id bringing your muddy shoes into the driver's car at the end of the hike.
 \n**UnRuffle/UnRavel:** To experience a time of quiet in a manner that you
  feel worthwhile. Démêlez votre stress.\nEngage the 5 senses (sight\, sm
 ell\, touch\, taste\, hearing)\,\nObserve the movement of the forest & wat
 er.\nBreathe the aroma of the air\, water\, plants and forest.\nFeel the t
 exture of the air\, water\, trees and plants.\nListening to the sound of a
 ir\, water\, critters & birds\;\nTaste the air of the breezes or soothing 
 snacks.\nAll hikes are at your own risk. You are responsible for your OWN 
 safety and adequate equipment.\nWaiver: The organizer of this event is a v
 olunteer and not a professional guide. The function of the organizer is on
 ly to organize this event. There are certain risks inherent in any outdoor
  activity. Each participant\, by signing up to attend this event\, agrees 
 to release from liability the leader(s)\, Hendo Fun Friends\, its Partners
 \, Affiliates\, and members for any accident\, injury\, illness\, or perso
 nal loss which might occur while participating in this activity or while t
 raveling in any vehicle during this trip. **Each participant further agree
 s to abide by the rules and regulations concerning safety\, to follow inst
 ructions of the leader(s)\, and not to become intentionally separated from
  the group.** The leader(s) also has the right to use any images collected
  on this trip for recording on website photo collections.\ngordie's contac
 t: curmudgeonhiker@gmail.com\n(**before** day of hike): 828.393.0297 (talk
  & text)\n**Pics: https://www.flickr.com/photos/146993931@N05/albums**
